# Cloudflare Pages SPA fallback.
#
# Only these paths get a real prerendered file at build time (see
# scripts/generate-static-pages.mjs): /, /docs, /blog and each blog post.
# Every other route is client-side only — App.tsx switches on
# window.location.pathname — so a static host must serve index.html for them or
# a direct hit / refresh / shared link 404s.
#
# nginx already does this via `try_files $uri $uri/ /index.html` (nginx.conf),
# so this file is inert on the Railway deployment and only matters wherever
# Cloudflare Pages serves the site. Harmless to have in both.
#
# Routes are listed EXPLICITLY rather than using a blanket `/* /index.html 200`:
# a catch-all would also swallow /api/*, /mcp and /metrics, which must reach the
# backend rather than return the SPA shell. Add a line here when you add a route
# to App.tsx that isn't prerendered.

/pricing            /index.html   200
/trust              /index.html   200
/design-partners    /index.html   200
/metrics-reference  /index.html   200
/terms              /index.html   200
/privacy            /index.html   200
/refund             /index.html   200
/sign-in            /index.html   200
/sign-up            /index.html   200
